---
description: Commit message style and no-secrets policy
alwaysApply: true
---

# Commits

- One or two sentences on why, not a file list.
- Never commit secrets, `.env`, credentials, or private keys.
- Only commit when the user asked, or when the current repo's documented plan includes a commit step the user already approved.
- Do not skip hooks (`--no-verify`) unless the user explicitly asked.
